    "title": "Man killed in Coosa County crash - NewsBreak",
    "text": "COOSA COUNTY, Ala. ( WIAT ) — A 62-year-old man was killed in a single-vehicle crash that occurred Wednesday evening in Coosa County, according to the Alabama Law Enforcement Agency. Edward L. Gilbert, of Equality, was killed when the Chevrolet Impala he was driving left the roadway and struck a tree. Gilbert was not using a seat belt at the time of the crash, and he was pronounced dead at the scene. The crash occurred on Alabama 22 near the 99 mile marker. Troopers with ALEA’s Highway Patrol Division are investigating the crash. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS 42.",
